Z||000003||Robert||06-13-2000||09:35 PM||||These wheels aren’t cheep.  The brand is Fittipaldi.   The tire size my customer had on his car was 235/45ZR17.  I’m going to check with my local tire store to see if they can get these wheels at a better price.<P><BR>Here is the site the picture is from <A HREF="http://www.keyway.net/~salesco/wheels/fittipaldi/fittipaldi_fitti_500_modular.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.keyway.net/~salesco/wheels/fittipaldi/fittipaldi_fitti_500_modular.htm</A> <P>Here is another site that sells the wheels<P> <A HREF="http://www.eliteone.com/wheels/fittipaldi.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.eliteone.com/wheels/fittipaldi.htm</A> <P>This site doesn’t sell the wheels, but it’s a lot fun looking at different wheel on a Fiero<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com/mycar/baseframeset.jsp?model=Fiero+GT&make=Pontiac&year=1987" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com/mycar/baseframeset.jsp?model=Fiero+GT&make=Pontiac&year=1987</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Robert (edited 06-13-2000).]||||reg||1
