Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-13-2000||10:48 PM||||yep, each thats what you get when you have a REAL modular wheel. 3 piece wheels ARE worth their weight in gold... they are available at <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>  in 17x7.5 for $435 each. Probly not as wide as the Mustang units... if you scrap the curb or hit somthing and just bend one side of the wheel you dont have to replace the entire thing.. just the broken or distorted section!!! and the weight savings! they keep more weight on the center of the rim making the rotating mass beter distributed for better acceleration and braking! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spyder||06-13-2000||11:09 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.jdwheels.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jdwheels.com</A> <BR>I bought my wheels from them, they were quick (two days and they were here) and a great price.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/wheelcompa.jpg"> <BR>I'm not sure if these will fit the stock bolt pattern because I'm using spacers and adapters. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||06-13-2000||11:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spyder:<BR><B>Check out <A HREF="http://www.jdwheels.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jdwheels.com</A> <BR>I bought my wheels from them, they were quick (two days and they were here) and a great price.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/wheelcompa.jpg">  <BR>I'm not sure if these will fit the stock bolt pattern because I'm using spacers and adapters. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What kind of adapters??<P>||||reg||5
Z||000010||Spyder||06-14-2000||01:23 AM||||I don’t know why I posted the pic, those wheels are on my Fiero kit car.<BR>I used spacer/adapters from Fred at <A HREF="http://www.wheeladapter.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wheeladapter.com</A> <BR>I not sure if there is enough space to use the adapters on the stock body.<BR>I had the hardest time finding good looking wheels, in the sizes that I wanted for the price I was willing to pay (or should I say afford). <BR>17x7.5 for $200.<BR>I guess the main point was <A HREF="http://www.jdwheels.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jdwheels.com</A>  was the best deal I could find on some good looking rims.<P>I also liked salesco prices but were not easy at all to deal with via two phone conversations.<P>Robert, <BR>I forgot to mention.<BR>I Love Those Wheels!!<p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 06-14-2000).]||||reg||1
